Linux 6.18 LTS for the Wyze Cam v2 (Ingenic T20). See docs/kernel-modern.md.

build.sh      fetches the pinned sources and toolchain into third_party/kernel/,
              builds build/kernel/out/{uImage,modules/,wyze-cam-v2.dtb,...}
config        kernel options on top of tinyconfig, grouped and commented
mkuimage.py   legacy U-Boot header for the LZMA kernel
dts/          T20 SoC and Wyze Cam v2 device trees (copied into the tree)
patches/      applied in order to Linux v6.18.59:
  0001-0005   gtxaspec/thingino-linux ingenic-7.1-rc1 (T31 on mainline):
              pinctrl and machine plumbing, the SFC SPI flash controller
              driver, an MMC clock fix. Unchanged; run.
  0006        T20 machine, Wyze Cam v2 board option. Ours; runs.
  0007        T20 CGU (clocks), from the vendor soc-t20/common/clk; the
              audio clock's M/N divider as mainline's X1000. Ours; runs.
  0008        T20 pinctrl, from the vendor soc-t20 gpio.c/platform.h. Ours;
              runs.
  0009        SFC: T20 compatible (X1000 registers). Ours; runs.
  0010        spi-nor: erase in 32 KiB blocks. Ours; runs.
  0011        JX-F22/JX-F23 sensor, V4L2 subdevice. Ours (register tables
              from Ingenic's GPL-2.0+ sensor drivers); runs (JX-F22).
  0012        T20 camera input and ISP, V4L2 (NV12 out, white balance,
              colour, two outputs, spatial and temporal noise reduction,
              sharpening), and the DVP pin group. Ours, from
              docs/t20-isp-hardware.md; runs.
  0013        T20 VPU JPEG and H.264 encoders, V4L2 mem2mem. Ours (VPU
              sequences and register names from Ingenic's GPL-2.0 drivers,
              the T20 H.264 values in docs/t20-isp-hardware.md); runs.
  0014        T20 AIC (mainline jz4740-i2s) and internal codec (microphone).
              Ours (codec sequences from Ingenic's GPL-2.0 OSS driver); runs.
  0015        dma-jz4780: no oops on the status of a terminated transfer
              (every close of a capture stream). Ours; runs.
Out of tree:  rtl8189fs (WiFi), jwrdegoede/rtl8189ES_linux 13bbdbc; runs.

All of it boots and runs on a Wyze Cam v2 (docs/kernel-modern.md, "Bring-up
on hardware").
